{
  "note": [
    "The Kalamontee Platform's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. KALAMONTEE-PLATFORM.metadata.json v2: 16 x 6 x 10, the eye at the middle -- LAWANDA-PLATFORM's accepted envelope, since two stations on one line sharing two cars are one piece of engineering.",
    "The game: \"a wide, flat strip of concrete which continues westward ... A faded sign on the wall reads \\\"Shutul Platform -- Kalamontee Staashun\\\"\" (compone.zil 3193-3200). North and south the platform's edge walls open 6.0 x 4.2 onto the berths, each centred 0.5 m off its car's door (Betty's at x -3, Alfie's at x 3, the accepted Lawanda offsets); each berth is a tube with its track bed 1.0 m down, the tunnel running EAST and a buffer wall at the dead end west of it (globals.zil 1702-1717). The cars are scripts/fabric-shuttle.mjs's, so both berths are drawn empty here and the four shuttle states wait on that file.",
    "West, the 4.0 x 2.6 portal onto the Waiting Area, the deck unbroken through it: its benches along its north wall and its west wall 20.2 m out. The red elevator door is NOT in sight -- the portal's far jamb holds every ray to the Waiting Area's south wall west of its own x -2.16, and the door's east edge is 0.46 m short of that -- so no door and no switch here, though the package's beyond text has it visible."
  ],
